From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chatkord <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adm-restart: the audio device comes back for the next call

libwebrtc terminates the media engine when its last peer connection is
destroyed and initializes it again for the next one. AdmProxy's Init was
a no-op, so the synthetic device's 10 ms pull never restarted and no
received track was handed a frame again until the process restarted.
Measured: a debugger on the window saw ~PeerConnection reach
SyntheticAudioDevice::Terminate as the call was left; the next call
received nothing, and the thread named SyntheticAudioD was gone.

Init now initializes the sub ADMs again; both are idempotent.

diff --git a/webrtc-sys/src/adm_proxy.cpp b/webrtc-sys/src/adm_proxy.cpp
index 2b4eacf..8acc700 100644
--- a/webrtc-sys/src/adm_proxy.cpp
+++ b/webrtc-sys/src/adm_proxy.cpp
@@ -351,8 +351,19 @@ int32_t AdmProxy::RegisterAudioCallback(webrtc::AudioTransport* transport) {
 }
 
 int32_t AdmProxy::Init() {
-  // Init is a no-op - the sub ADMs are initialized at creation time
-  return 0;
+  // The engine terminates its device after its last connection and initializes
+  // it for the next, so the sub ADMs come back here; both Inits are idempotent.
+  return RunOnWorker([this] {
+    RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(worker_thread_);
+    int32_t result = synthetic_adm_ ? synthetic_adm_->Init() : 0;
+    // The engine aborts on a failed Init: a platform ADM that cannot come back
+    // is logged and left out, as at its creation, and the synthetic one serves.
+    if (platform_adm_ && platform_adm_->Init() != 0) {
+      RTC_LOG(LS_ERROR) << "AdmProxy: Platform ADM Init() failed again";
+      platform_adm_ = nullptr;
+    }
+    return result;
+  });
 }
 
 int32_t AdmProxy::Terminate() {
